In our method, a large batch size is required to train the generator~\cite{brock2018large} and ensure the accuracy of the discrepancy estimation. To explore the influence of different batch sizes, we conduct several experiments on classification and semantic segmentation datasets. As illustrated in Fig.~\ref{batch-size}, a small batch size injures the performance of student models. We also found that increasing batch size can bring tremendous benefits to our method. An important reason for the phenomenon is that the large batch size can provide sufficient statistical information for hard sample generation and make the training more stable.

