We provide more visualization results in this section. Fig.~\ref{vis-cls} and Fig.~\ref{caltech101-vis} compare the generated samples with real samples on classification datasets. Those fake samples can not be recognized by humans, but indeed contain sufficient knowledge for their tasks. Fig.~\ref{vis-seg} provides some generated samples on segmentation datasets, as well as the predictions produced by teacher models.
To further demonstrate the effectiveness of our method, we provide more segmentation results in Fig.~\ref{seg-camvid} and Fig.~\ref{seg-nyuv2}. As in the main paper, our data-free method is compared with several data-driven baselines, such as KD-REL and KD-UNR. KD-REL requires related data and KD-UNR uses some unrelated data. 

